{# Shared price rendering for the public menu — used at both render sites
   (front + back of the flip card). A
   product with variants renders one stacked row per price (label
   left/muted, price right, currency on every row) — see
   .price-stack/.price-row/.price-item-label/.price-item-value in each
   layout's own <style> block. A simple product (no variants) renders as a
   single plain text price. Both paths show $currencyDisplay (the symbol
   when exactly one supported currency uses it, otherwise the code — see
   MenuPreferencesResolver::getCurrencyDisplay()) rather than the raw
   $currency code, so a menu mixing simple and variant-priced dishes shows
   one consistent currency label throughout instead of "12.00 EUR" next to
   "12.00 €". See also Product::hasPriceVariants().

   Right-to-left menus (menu_dir(locale) == 'rtl'): every amount + its
   currency (+ a supplement's leading "+") is wrapped in
   <bdi dir="ltr" class="price-ltr"> as one unit, so the bidi algorithm
   can't move the currency or the "+" to the other side of the digits. It
   sits INSIDE .price-item-value, which keeps the page's direction — its
   text-align:end still means the outer edge. Left-to-right menus render
   exactly the markup they always did (ltrOpen/ltrClose are empty).
   Price labels (owner text, never translated) get <span dir="auto"> on
   RTL menus for the same reason as show.html.twig's autoOpen. #}
{% macro price(product, currency, showCurrency, currencyDisplay, locale) %}{% set ltrOpen = menu_dir(locale) == 'rtl' ? '<bdi dir="ltr" class="price-ltr">' : '' %}{% set ltrClose = ltrOpen ? '</bdi>' : '' %}{% set autoOpen = ltrOpen ? '<span dir="auto">' : '' %}{% set autoClose = ltrOpen ? '</span>' : '' %}{% if product.hasPriceVariants %}<span class="price-stack"><span class="price-row">{% if product.basePriceLabel %}<span class="price-item-label">{{ autoOpen|raw }}{{ product.basePriceLabel }}{{ autoClose|raw }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="price-item-value">{{ ltrOpen|raw }}{{ (product.convertedPrice / 100)|menu_number(locale) }}{% if showCurrency %}<span class="price-currency">{{ currencyDisplay }}</span>{% endif %}{{ ltrClose|raw }}</span></span>{% for variant in product.priceVariants %}<span class="price-row"><span class="price-item-label">{{ autoOpen|raw }}{{ variant.label }}{{ autoClose|raw }}</span><span class="price-item-value">{{ ltrOpen|raw }}{{ (product.getConvertedVariantPrice(variant) / 100)|menu_number(locale) }}{% if showCurrency %}<span class="price-currency">{{ currencyDisplay }}</span>{% endif %}{{ ltrClose|raw }}</span></span>{% endfor %}</span>{% else %}{{ ltrOpen|raw }}{{ (product.convertedPrice / 100)|menu_number(locale) }}{% if showCurrency %}<span class="price-currency">{{ currencyDisplay }}</span>{% endif %}{{ ltrClose|raw }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{# One amount in cents, formatted exactly like price()'s single-price path
   (same |menu_number, same .price-currency suffix). Used by oneLine() below
   for the banner's "Desde" + lowest-price line. #}
{% macro amount(cents, currencyDisplay, locale) %}{% set ltrOpen = menu_dir(locale) == 'rtl' ? '<bdi dir="ltr" class="price-ltr">' : '' %}{% set ltrClose = ltrOpen ? '</bdi>' : '' %}{{ ltrOpen|raw }}{{ (cents / 100)|menu_number(locale) }}<span class="price-currency">{{ currencyDisplay }}</span>{{ ltrClose|raw }}{% endmacro %}
{# A dish's "+X €" supplement amount — the one markup behind every
   .dish-supplement/.row-supplement/.dish-detail-supplement in the layout
   and the banner's bannerSupplement() below. #}
{% macro supplement(product, currencyDisplay, locale) %}{% set ltrOpen = menu_dir(locale) == 'rtl' ? '<bdi dir="ltr" class="price-ltr">' : '' %}{% set ltrClose = ltrOpen ? '</bdi>' : '' %}{{ ltrOpen|raw }}<span class="suppl-value">+{{ (product.getConvertedSupplementPrice() / 100)|menu_number(locale) }}</span><span class="price-currency">{{ currencyDisplay }}</span>{{ ltrClose|raw }}{% endmacro %}
{# The maison recommendation banner's supplement line
   (themes/maison/_banner_text.html.twig). Same text as the list's
   .dish-supplement; "· +X €" is wrapped in .suppl-amount so the banner can
   keep it together (white-space: nowrap in maison/overrides.html.twig) — a
   break then falls before the "·", never after. #}
{% macro bannerSupplement(product, currencyDisplay, locale) %}<div class="dish-supplement">{{ 'dish.supplement'|trans({}, 'menu_public', locale) }} <span class="suppl-amount">· {{ _self.supplement(product, currencyDisplay, locale) }}</span></div>{% endmacro %}
{# One-line price for the maison chef's-recommendation banner
   (themes/maison/_banner_text.html.twig). Multiprice → "Desde" + the lowest
   price: base price + every variant, converted; all equal → just the
   price. Single price → price()'s own single-price output. #}
{% macro oneLine(product, currency, currencyDisplay, locale) %}{% if product.hasPriceVariants %}{% set prices = [product.convertedPrice]|merge(product.priceVariants|map(v => product.getConvertedVariantPrice(v))) %}{% if min(prices) != max(prices) %}<span class="price-from">{{ 'dish.price_from'|trans({}, 'menu_public', locale) }}</span> {% endif %}{{ _self.amount(min(prices), currencyDisplay, locale) }}{% else %}{{ _self.price(product, currency, true, currencyDisplay, locale) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
